// A trailing `if` is a condition only when the rest of the line is a whole
// expression, up to the end of the line, a comment, `->`, `{` or `#`.
// Otherwise the line stays narration, whatever words follow the `if`.

state
  ok: true
  missing: false

character bob
  name: Bob

beat Start
  Tell me if it is true.

  I would, if not now.

  Tell me if you and I agree.

  This is not a drill.

  not now, please.

  is it you?

  Ask if the door is open.

  Run if (really) you must.

  bob: I wonder if it is.

  Shown if ok

  Hidden if not ok

  Shown too if ok and not missing // comment after the condition

  bob: Also shown if ok is true

  if ok and not missing
    Statement shown.

  choice
    Go if ok and not missing -> End
    Stay if (ok) or missing
      Stayed.

beat End
  Arrived.

/*
<test>
- choices: [0]
  expected: |
    ~ Tell me if it is true.

    ~ I would, if not now.

    ~ Tell me if you and I agree.

    ~ This is not a drill.

    ~ not now, please.

    ~ is it you?

    ~ Ask if the door is open.

    ~ Run if (really) you must.

    Bob: I wonder if it is.

    ~ Shown

    ~ Shown too

    Bob: Also shown

    ~ Statement shown.

    + Go
    + Stay

    ~ Arrived.
</test>
